electron/laya — vendored Laya implementation
==========================================

Vendored from laya-mlx (Apache-2.0):
  Repository: https://github.com/mizchi/laya-mlx
  Source revision: dc3aa6b150cb861d0788fbd421cfd1303de4ed57
  Source directory: web/packages/laya-web/src

The following seven files are copied from that revision with import specifier
changes ("./x.ts" -> "./x", see README.md) and a provenance header added:

  types.ts
  pyjson.ts
  tokenizer.ts
  questions.ts
  prompt.ts
  calibration.ts
  agent.ts

Local performance changes to tokenizer.ts, prompt.ts and agent.ts are adapted
from nizitao's WechatVibe PR #26:
  https://github.com/tswawa/WechatVibe/pull/26
  Source revision: bca5c5ab4258e16340b5a4ecea94d070011853a9

  tokenizer.ts  Bounded FIFO encode memoization, equivalent Unicode whitespace
                membership and indexed token accumulation. This integration
                also freezes returned ids, caps raw-text key length and exposes
                explicit cache clearing for account/model/cache lifecycle events.
  prompt.ts     Optional immutable precomputed state ids in buildSequence.
  agent.ts      Encode each shared state once per prepare, lazily for nonempty
                question sets.

The offline tests in tests/laya-tokenizer.test.ts are adapted from the same
contribution and extended for immutable results, cache limits and clearing.
They use synthetic tokenizers and do not measure production model performance.

The tokenizer/sequence/answer parity test fixture
(tests/fixtures/laya-parity-multilingual.json) is also copied from that
revision, file web/fixtures/parity-multilingual.json.

